@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# G1 launcher repair candidate, preparation only
+
+This is a separate post-failure launcher preparation candidate. It is not an execution release, a second G1 attempt or a new scientific protocol ID. The original stopped invocation, original frozen bundle, generated bytecode, reviews and all failed evidence remain unchanged.
+
+The only execution-path addition is launch.sh. It invokes the caller-specified, separately hash-verified existing Python interpreter with -B before run_gamma.py or any frozen-bundle module is imported. Python's interpreter-level bytecode-write suppression therefore applies to the initial control_common import. Existing late child environment suppression remains unchanged. -B does not prevent Python from reading an existing cache; exact recursive coverage must continue rejecting every unexpected cache/importable artifact. No file allowlist, source verification, anchor, deadline, thread, scientific input, point, threshold, numerical implementation or process guard is relaxed.
+
+Use the shell launcher with MATTERLAB_PYTHON bound to the verified existing interpreter. Do not call run_gamma.py directly as the proposed repaired launch path. This candidate's freeze status is launcher_repair_preparation_only, so the unchanged controller rejects it after bundle verification and before reading any release or claiming any anchor. The frozen scientific protocol and protocol.json retain their exact previous bytes. The implementation manifest adds this note and launch.sh; the new freeze binds that manifest and its prior freeze provenance. No previously issued review attests the new manifest.
+
+Metadata-only tests use the actual shell launcher and unchanged candidate controller, a nonexistent release, and this non-executable status. The clean candidate must reach the explicit Not reviewed/released rejection without creating any cache or changing a member. Separate preserved fixture copies containing unexpected Python source or bytecode must fail the unchanged exact-coverage gate. Additional tests may inspect interpreter sys.flags and environment behavior with dummy code; no model import, construction or forward, child preflight/inference, real release or protocol anchor is permitted. Metadata tests have a 10-second per-process timeout; their cumulative wall time is recorded and is not physical calculation time.
+
+The prior controller invocation remains stopped on exception. Its anchor was not reached, but absence is not permission to reuse the stopped release. This repair does not assign a new protocol ID, change the original no-retry rule, renew any resource clock or authorize another invocation for science. Any future scientific continuation requires a separately recorded parent decision resolving the stopped-release/no-retry boundary, exact reviewed bindings, fresh gates and an explicit resource-stage definition. If that decision conflicts with immutable protocol semantics, execution remains blocked. No automatic status promotion or evaluation follows these tests.
+
+The preparation admission and deadline are preserved privately, separate from the earlier scientific investigation clock. Existing numerical failures, unrun historical C2, limited P1 repeatability, incomplete migration, fallback and single schedule remain unchanged. This candidate makes no new physical measurement or material claim.
